v0.9b4 2026-09-17
- No energy-accounting algorithm changes from v0.9b2/v0.9b3.
- Replaced the v3.79-only install lock with fail-closed structural compatibility checks for later Venus OS versions; minimum version v3.79.
- Known hashes identify field-validated sources. Structural compatibility alone does not establish field validation.
- Added tools/preflight.sh to check source compatibility before installation or reinstallation.
- Added tools/feature.sh to toggle Fix 3 and Fix 4 in persistent configuration and restart the affected service.

v0.9b3 2026-09-16
- No energy-accounting algorithm changes from v0.9b2.
- Added a check for a changed vrmlogger process ID after installation and removal; service health must be checked separately.
- Disabled optional features and left input-role overrides empty in the default configuration for reuse on other systems.
- Documented SetupHelper 9.4 reinstallation after firmware updates and stopping installation when compatibility checks fail.
- Added tools/status.sh for maintenance checks.

v0.9b2 2026-09-16
- Fixed patch validation on Venus OS by using SetupHelper's full patch utility instead of BusyBox patch, with the installer's forward/reverse handling.

v0.9b1 2026-09-16
- Combined four energy-accounting fixes into one SetupHelper package.
- Moved runtime settings to persistent SetupHelper configuration, replacing Node-RED/state-file controls.
- Added v3.79/source-hash checks and Python compilation checks before installation.
- Documented sampling-interval matching for cross-VE.Bus energy, load-meter scope and tested versus untested scenarios.
